<!DOCTYPE html>
<html><head><meta charset="utf-8"><title>KFPL All Pages Backend API Handoff</title>
<style>body{font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:#172033;line-height:1.42;margin:38px}h1{color:#1d4ed8;border-bottom:3px solid #1d4ed8;padding-bottom:10px}h2{color:#1e40af;border-bottom:1px solid #bfdbfe;padding-bottom:5px;margin-top:30px}h3{color:#334155;margin-top:22px}h4{color:#475569;margin-bottom:5px}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;margin:10px 0 18px}th{background:#1e3a8a;color:#fff;text-align:left}th,td{border:1px solid #cbd5e1;padding:7px;vertical-align:top}pre{font-family:Consolas,monospace;background:#f1f5f9;border:1px solid #cbd5e1;padding:10px;white-space:pre-wrap}code{font-family:Consolas,monospace}.note{background:#eff6ff;border-left:4px solid #2563eb;padding:10px}.warn{background:#fff7ed;border-left:4px solid #f97316;padding:10px}.small{font-size:11px;color:#475569}</style></head><body>
<h1>KFPL B2B Marketplace — Complete Backend API Handoff</h1>
<p><b>Audience:</b> Backend/API development team</p><p><b>Purpose:</b> Define the API flow for every current Buyer, Supplier, Admin, Authentication, Messaging, Catalog, Order, RFQ, Payment, Inventory, Review, Support, Notification, Analytics, and Profile page.</p>
<div class="note"><b>Core relationship:</b><br>Users create or browse Products. Buyers create RFQs. Suppliers submit Quotations. Buyers accept quotations and create Orders. Admins govern users, catalog, orders, inventory, payments, reviews, support, and notifications.</div>

<h2>1. API conventions</h2>
<pre>Base URL: /api/v1
Admin URL: /api/v1/admin
Buyer URL: /api/v1/buyer
Supplier URL: /api/v1/supplier
Shared URL: /api/v1</pre>
<p>Every protected request uses:</p><pre>Authorization: Bearer &lt;access_token&gt;
Content-Type: application/json</pre>
<table><tr><th>HTTP status</th><th>Meaning</th></tr><tr><td>200</td><td>Successful read/update</td></tr><tr><td>201</td><td>Successful create</td></tr><tr><td>204</td><td>Successful delete/archive with no body</td></tr><tr><td>400</td><td>Validation error</td></tr><tr><td>401</td><td>Missing/expired token</td></tr><tr><td>403</td><td>Insufficient permission</td></tr><tr><td>404</td><td>Resource not found</td></tr><tr><td>409</td><td>Duplicate/conflicting resource</td></tr><tr><td>422</td><td>Business rule violation</td></tr><tr><td>500</td><td>Unexpected server error</td></tr></table>
<p>List APIs should support <code>page</code>, <code>limit</code>, <code>search</code>, filters, sorting, and return a pagination object.</p>
<pre>{"success":true,"data":[],"pagination":{"page":1,"limit":20,"total":0,"totalPages":0}}</pre>
<p>Use UTC ISO timestamps. Store currency amounts in minor units or fixed decimal numeric columns. Prefer soft delete/archive for business records. Add audit logs for admin mutations.</p>

<h2>2. Authentication, onboarding, and session flow</h2>
<h3>2.1 Send OTP / verify phone</h3><pre>POST /api/v1/auth/otp/send
POST /api/v1/auth/otp/verify</pre>
<pre>POST /api/v1/auth/otp/send
{"phone":"+919876543210","purpose":"LOGIN"}

POST /api/v1/auth/otp/verify
{"phone":"+919876543210","otp":"123456","deviceId":"device_123"}</pre>
<p>Verify OTP, create or locate the user, issue access and refresh tokens, and return whether onboarding is complete.</p>
<h3>2.2 Login, logout, refresh</h3><pre>POST /api/v1/auth/login
POST /api/v1/auth/refresh
POST /api/v1/auth/logout
GET  /api/v1/auth/me</pre>
<h3>2.3 Onboarding</h3><pre>POST /api/v1/onboarding/profile
PATCH /api/v1/users/me
POST /api/v1/users/me/gst/verify
POST /api/v1/users/me/documents
GET  /api/v1/users/me/onboarding-status</pre>
<p>Profile fields include name, phone, email, companyName, businessType, activeRole, GST number, location, address, avatar, KYC status, and language.</p>
<h3>2.4 Role switch</h3><pre>PATCH /api/v1/users/me/active-role
{"activeRole":"BUYER"}</pre>
<p>Allowed roles: BUYER, SUPPLIER, or BUYER_SUPPLIER depending on the account permissions.</p>

<h2>3. Shared user/profile APIs</h2>
<pre>GET   /api/v1/users/me
PATCH /api/v1/users/me
POST  /api/v1/users/me/avatar
GET   /api/v1/users/me/addresses
POST  /api/v1/users/me/addresses
PATCH /api/v1/users/me/addresses/:addressId
DELETE /api/v1/users/me/addresses/:addressId
PATCH /api/v1/users/me/preferences
GET   /api/v1/users/me/notifications</pre>
<p>Validate email, phone, GST, address, and avatar. Do not allow a user to update KYC status or financial balances directly.</p>

<h2>4. Catalog and product APIs</h2>
<h3>4.1 Catalog hierarchy</h3><pre>Category
  └── Subcategory
        └── Product</pre>
<p>Category and Subcategory are separate resources. Product creation must reference both IDs.</p>
<h3>4.2 Images</h3><pre>POST /api/v1/admin/catalog/images
Content-Type: multipart/form-data
Fields: file, type=CATEGORY|SUBCATEGORY|PRODUCT</pre>
<h3>4.3 Categories</h3><pre>GET    /api/v1/admin/catalog/categories
POST   /api/v1/admin/catalog/categories
GET    /api/v1/admin/catalog/categories/:categoryId
PATCH  /api/v1/admin/catalog/categories/:categoryId
DELETE /api/v1/admin/catalog/categories/:categoryId</pre>
<p>Category create payload:</p><pre>{"name":"Dairy, Bread &amp; Eggs","imageUrl":"https://cdn/.../dairy.jpg","description":"Fresh dairy products","displayOrder":1,"discount":5,"isActive":true}</pre>
<p>Category name and image are mandatory. Description, displayOrder, discount, and isActive are stored and editable.</p>
<h3>4.4 Subcategories</h3><pre>GET    /api/v1/admin/catalog/subcategories
POST   /api/v1/admin/catalog/subcategories
GET    /api/v1/admin/catalog/categories/:categoryId/subcategories
GET    /api/v1/admin/catalog/subcategories/:subcategoryId
PATCH  /api/v1/admin/catalog/subcategories/:subcategoryId
DELETE /api/v1/admin/catalog/subcategories/:subcategoryId</pre>
<p>Subcategory create payload:</p><pre>{"categoryId":"cat_dairy","name":"Milk","imageUrl":"https://cdn/.../milk.jpg","description":"Toned and full cream milk","displayOrder":1,"discount":3,"isActive":true}</pre>
<p>Subcategory name and image are mandatory. The selected category must exist and be active.</p>
<h3>4.5 Products</h3><pre>GET    /api/v1/catalog/products
GET    /api/v1/catalog/products/:productId
GET    /api/v1/admin/catalog/products
POST   /api/v1/admin/catalog/products
PATCH  /api/v1/admin/catalog/products/:productId
DELETE /api/v1/admin/catalog/products/:productId</pre>
<p>Product create payload:</p><pre>{
  "productName":"Amul Taaza Milk",
  "categoryId":"cat_dairy",
  "subcategoryId":"sub_milk",
  "brand":"Amul",
  "description":"Fresh toned milk",
  "imageUrl":"https://cdn/.../amul-milk.jpg",
  "price":30,
  "mrp":32,
  "quantity":500,
  "unit":"ml",
  "stockQuantity":50,
  "status":"ACTIVE",
  "sku":"AML-MILK-500"
}</pre>
<p>Product rules: category and subcategory must be active and related; SKU must be unique; price must be greater than zero; MRP must be greater than or equal to price; unit must be ml, g, kg, or piece; stock must be non-negative; discount should be calculated by the server.</p>
<pre>discountPercentage = ((mrp - price) / mrp) * 100</pre>
<h3>4.6 Product listing filters</h3><pre>GET /api/v1/admin/catalog/products?search=milk&amp;categoryId=cat_dairy&amp;subcategoryId=sub_milk&amp;stockStatus=IN_STOCK&amp;status=ACTIVE&amp;page=1&amp;limit=20</pre>
<p>Products page should return image, product name, category, subcategory, brand, price, stock, status, and actions. Buyer product listing should hide drafts, archived items, and inactive catalog nodes.</p>

<h2>5. Buyer application pages</h2>
<h3>5.1 Buyer Home</h3><pre>GET /api/v1/buyer/home
GET /api/v1/catalog/categories?isActive=true
GET /api/v1/catalog/products?featured=true
GET /api/v1/buyer/recommendations</pre>
<p>Return category cards, featured products, recently viewed products, verified suppliers, and buyer-specific recommendations.</p>
<h3>5.2 Explore/Search</h3><pre>GET /api/v1/catalog/products
  ?search=&amp;categoryId=&amp;minPrice=&amp;maxPrice=&amp;moqMax=&amp;location=&amp;gstVerified=&amp;verifiedSupplier=&amp;sortBy=&amp;page=&amp;limit=</pre>
<p>Supported sorting: relevance, price_low, price_high, rating, and MOQ. Return product cards with image, title, brand, supplier, rating, price tiers, MOQ, stock availability, and wishlist state.</p>
<h3>5.3 Product detail</h3><pre>GET  /api/v1/catalog/products/:productId
POST /api/v1/buyer/products/:productId/view
POST /api/v1/buyer/wishlist/:productId
DELETE /api/v1/buyer/wishlist/:productId
GET  /api/v1/buyer/wishlist</pre>
<p>Product detail returns images, description, specifications, price tiers, supplier verification, rating, stock, and related products.</p>
<h3>5.4 Buyer RFQ Desk</h3><pre>GET /api/v1/buyer/rfqs
GET /api/v1/buyer/rfqs/:rfqId
POST /api/v1/buyer/rfqs
PATCH /api/v1/buyer/rfqs/:rfqId/cancel
GET /api/v1/buyer/rfqs/:rfqId/quotations</pre>
<p>Create RFQ payload:</p><pre>{"productId":"prod_123","productTitle":"Amul Taaza Milk","categoryId":"cat_dairy","quantity":50,"unit":"piece","targetPrice":28,"expectedDeliveryDate":"2026-09-01","description":"Need regular supply","attachments":[]}</pre>
<p>RFQ statuses: OPEN, QUOTED, ACCEPTED, EXPIRED, REJECTED. Creating an RFQ should notify eligible suppliers.</p>
<h3>5.5 RFQ comparison and quotation acceptance</h3><pre>GET  /api/v1/buyer/rfqs/:rfqId/quotations/compare
POST /api/v1/buyer/rfqs/:rfqId/quotations/:quotationId/accept
POST /api/v1/buyer/rfqs/:rfqId/quotations/:quotationId/reject</pre>
<p>Accepting a quotation should be transactional and should create an order or return a payment/order creation token, depending on the checkout design.</p>
<h3>5.6 Buyer Orders</h3><pre>GET /api/v1/buyer/orders?status=ALL|SHIPPED|DELIVERED|CANCELLED
GET /api/v1/buyer/orders/:orderId
POST /api/v1/buyer/orders/:orderId/cancel
POST /api/v1/buyer/orders/:orderId/confirm-delivery
GET /api/v1/buyer/orders/:orderId/tracking</pre>
<p>Return order number, product image, supplier, quantity, unit price, total amount, order date, status, payment status, delivery address, and tracking information.</p>

<h2>6. Supplier application pages</h2>
<h3>6.1 Supplier Dashboard</h3><pre>GET /api/v1/supplier/dashboard
GET /api/v1/supplier/analytics/summary
GET /api/v1/supplier/products?limit=5
GET /api/v1/supplier/rfqs?status=OPEN&amp;limit=5
GET /api/v1/supplier/orders?limit=5</pre>
<p>Dashboard metrics: today leads, today revenue, today orders, visitors, performance score, sales history, and top products.</p>
<h3>6.2 Supplier Products</h3><pre>GET    /api/v1/supplier/products
POST   /api/v1/supplier/products
GET    /api/v1/supplier/products/:productId
PATCH  /api/v1/supplier/products/:productId
DELETE /api/v1/supplier/products/:productId</pre>
<p>Supplier product create includes title, category, subcategory, brand, images, description, MOQ, unit, tierPricing, stock, specifications, supplier location, GST verification, and status. New products should enter PENDING approval when platform governance requires approval.</p>
<pre>{"title":"Servo Motor","categoryId":"cat_machinery","subcategoryId":"sub_motors","brand":"Apex","images":[],"description":"Industrial motor","moq":10,"unit":"piece","tierPricing":[{"minQty":10,"maxQty":49,"pricePerUnit":120},{"minQty":50,"maxQty":null,"pricePerUnit":95}],"stock":500,"status":"DRAFT"}</pre>
<h3>6.3 Supplier Leads/RFQs</h3><pre>GET  /api/v1/supplier/leads
GET  /api/v1/supplier/leads/:rfqId
POST /api/v1/supplier/leads/:rfqId/quotation
GET  /api/v1/supplier/quotations
PATCH /api/v1/supplier/quotations/:quotationId</pre>
<p>Quotation payload:</p><pre>{"rfqId":"rfq_123","unitPrice":28,"totalPrice":1400,"moq":50,"estimatedDeliveryDays":5,"shippingCost":100,"gstPercent":18,"notes":"Dispatch within 48 hours","validUntil":"2026-08-31"}</pre>
<p>Quotation statuses: PENDING, ACCEPTED, REJECTED. A supplier can quote only an open RFQ.</p>

<h2>7. Chat and messaging pages</h2>
<pre>GET  /api/v1/conversations
POST /api/v1/conversations
GET  /api/v1/conversations/:conversationId/messages?cursor=
POST /api/v1/conversations/:conversationId/messages
POST /api/v1/conversations/:conversationId/read
POST /api/v1/conversations/:conversationId/attachments</pre>
<p>Message types: TEXT, PRODUCT_CARD, QUOTATION_CARD, IMAGE, DOCUMENT. Validate that the sender belongs to the conversation. Use WebSocket events for realtime delivery if required:</p><pre>conversation.message.created
conversation.message.read
conversation.typing</pre>

<h2>8. Order, checkout, payment, and escrow flow</h2>
<h3>8.1 Order creation</h3><pre>POST /api/v1/orders
GET  /api/v1/orders/:orderId
GET  /api/v1/orders/:orderId/timeline</pre>
<p>Order creation is normally triggered by an accepted quotation.</p><pre>{"rfqId":"rfq_123","quotationId":"quote_123","items":[{"productId":"prod_123","quantity":50}],"deliveryAddressId":"addr_123","paymentMethod":"ONLINE"}</pre>
<h3>8.2 Payment</h3><pre>POST /api/v1/payments/create-intent
POST /api/v1/payments/:paymentId/confirm
POST /api/v1/payments/webhook
GET  /api/v1/payments/:paymentId
GET  /api/v1/orders/:orderId/payment</pre>
<p>Use idempotency keys on payment and order creation. Never mark a payment successful from the frontend; rely on the payment provider webhook.</p>
<h3>8.3 Order status lifecycle</h3><pre>PENDING → CONFIRMED → PROCESSING → SHIPPED → DELIVERED
Any eligible state → CANCELLED</pre>
<p>Supplier/admin actions:</p><pre>PATCH /api/v1/supplier/orders/:orderId/status
PATCH /api/v1/admin/orders/:orderId/status
POST  /api/v1/orders/:orderId/tracking</pre>
<p>Order payment statuses: PAID, PENDING, ESCROW_HOLD. Release escrow only after the configured delivery/return condition.</p>

<h2>9. Admin pages</h2>
<h3>9.1 Admin authentication</h3><pre>POST /api/v1/admin/auth/login
POST /api/v1/admin/auth/logout
POST /api/v1/admin/auth/refresh
GET  /api/v1/admin/auth/me</pre>
<p>Admin roles include Super Admin, Catalog Manager, Order &amp; Escrow Lead, Finance Admin, and Support Lead. Enforce server-side module permissions.</p>
<h3>9.2 Admin Dashboard</h3><pre>GET /api/v1/admin/dashboard/summary
GET /api/v1/admin/dashboard/sales-overview
GET /api/v1/admin/dashboard/order-status-breakdown
GET /api/v1/admin/dashboard/top-regions
GET /api/v1/admin/dashboard/latest-sales</pre>
<p>Return KPI cards, sales chart series, regional sales, order status counts, latest sales, revenue, users, pending approvals, and inventory alerts.</p>
<h3>9.3 User Management</h3><pre>GET   /api/v1/admin/users?role=BUYER|SUPPLIER&amp;search=&amp;status=&amp;page=&amp;limit=
GET   /api/v1/admin/users/:userId
PATCH /api/v1/admin/users/:userId/status
PATCH /api/v1/admin/users/:userId/role
POST  /api/v1/admin/roles/users
GET   /api/v1/admin/roles/users</pre>
<h3>9.4 Seller Management</h3><pre>GET   /api/v1/admin/sellers
GET   /api/v1/admin/sellers/applications
GET   /api/v1/admin/sellers/applications/:applicationId
POST  /api/v1/admin/sellers/applications/:applicationId/approve
POST  /api/v1/admin/sellers/applications/:applicationId/reject
GET   /api/v1/admin/sellers/stores
GET   /api/v1/admin/sellers/:sellerId/verification</pre>
<p>Seller application statuses: PENDING, APPROVED, REJECTED. Store and GST/KYC verification must be auditable.</p>
<h3>9.5 Buyer Management</h3><pre>GET /api/v1/admin/buyers
GET /api/v1/admin/buyers/:buyerId
GET /api/v1/admin/buyers/:buyerId/activity
PATCH /api/v1/admin/buyers/:buyerId/status</pre>
<h3>9.6 Catalog Governance</h3><pre>Use the Category, Subcategory, Product, Product Approval, and Brand APIs defined in Section 4.</pre>
<p>Product approval APIs:</p><pre>GET  /api/v1/admin/catalog/product-approvals?status=PENDING
GET  /api/v1/admin/catalog/product-approvals/:approvalId
POST /api/v1/admin/catalog/product-approvals/:approvalId/approve
POST /api/v1/admin/catalog/product-approvals/:approvalId/reject</pre>
<p>Brand registry APIs:</p><pre>GET   /api/v1/admin/catalog/brands
POST  /api/v1/admin/catalog/brands
PATCH /api/v1/admin/catalog/brands/:brandId
DELETE /api/v1/admin/catalog/brands/:brandId</pre>
<h3>9.7 Admin Orders</h3><pre>GET   /api/v1/admin/orders?status=&amp;paymentStatus=&amp;search=&amp;page=&amp;limit=
GET   /api/v1/admin/orders/:orderId
PATCH /api/v1/admin/orders/:orderId/status
POST  /api/v1/admin/orders/:orderId/tracking
GET   /api/v1/admin/orders/export</pre>
<h3>9.8 Admin RFQs and Quotations</h3><pre>GET /api/v1/admin/rfqs?status=&amp;search=&amp;page=&amp;limit=
GET /api/v1/admin/rfqs/:rfqId
GET /api/v1/admin/rfqs/:rfqId/quotations
GET /api/v1/admin/quotations?status=&amp;search=&amp;page=&amp;limit=
GET /api/v1/admin/quotations/:quotationId</pre>
<h3>9.9 Inventory</h3><pre>GET   /api/v1/admin/inventory?status=IN_STOCK|LOW_STOCK|CRITICAL
GET   /api/v1/admin/inventory/:inventoryId
PATCH /api/v1/admin/inventory/:inventoryId/stock
POST  /api/v1/admin/inventory/:inventoryId/adjustment</pre>
<p>Stock status rule:</p><pre>CRITICAL: availableStock &lt;= reorderLevel / 2
LOW_STOCK: availableStock &lt;= reorderLevel
IN_STOCK: availableStock &gt; reorderLevel</pre>
<h3>9.10 Payments and escrow</h3><pre>GET /api/v1/admin/payments?status=&amp;search=&amp;page=&amp;limit=
GET /api/v1/admin/payments/:paymentId
GET /api/v1/admin/escrow/settlements
POST /api/v1/admin/escrow/:escrowId/release
POST /api/v1/admin/escrow/:escrowId/hold
POST /api/v1/admin/escrow/:escrowId/refund</pre>
<h3>9.11 Reviews and ratings</h3><pre>GET   /api/v1/admin/reviews?status=PUBLISHED|FLAGGED|HIDDEN
GET   /api/v1/admin/reviews/:reviewId
PATCH /api/v1/admin/reviews/:reviewId/status
POST  /api/v1/products/:productId/reviews
GET   /api/v1/products/:productId/reviews</pre>
<h3>9.12 Support and disputes</h3><pre>GET   /api/v1/admin/support/tickets?status=&amp;priority=&amp;search=
GET   /api/v1/admin/support/tickets/:ticketId
POST  /api/v1/support/tickets
POST  /api/v1/admin/support/tickets/:ticketId/reply
PATCH /api/v1/admin/support/tickets/:ticketId/status
PATCH /api/v1/admin/support/tickets/:ticketId/priority</pre>
<p>Ticket statuses: OPEN, IN_PROGRESS, RESOLVED. Store conversation history and attachments.</p>
<h3>9.13 Notifications and broadcasts</h3><pre>GET  /api/v1/admin/notifications
POST /api/v1/admin/notifications
GET  /api/v1/admin/notifications/:notificationId
POST /api/v1/admin/notifications/:notificationId/send
POST /api/v1/admin/notifications/:notificationId/cancel</pre>
<p>Notification fields: title, message, audience, channels, scheduledAt, status. Statuses: SCHEDULED, DISPATCHED, CANCELLED.</p>
<h3>9.14 Analytics</h3><pre>GET /api/v1/admin/analytics/overview?from=&amp;to=&amp;groupBy=day|week|month
GET /api/v1/admin/analytics/sales
GET /api/v1/admin/analytics/products
GET /api/v1/admin/analytics/users
GET /api/v1/admin/analytics/regions</pre>
<h3>9.15 Admin profile/settings</h3><pre>GET   /api/v1/admin/profile
PATCH /api/v1/admin/profile
PATCH /api/v1/admin/settings
GET   /api/v1/admin/audit-logs?entityType=&amp;action=&amp;from=&amp;to=</pre>

<h2>10. Status transitions</h2>
<table><tr><th>Entity</th><th>Statuses</th><th>Important transition rule</th></tr>
<tr><td>Product</td><td>DRAFT, ACTIVE, OUT_OF_STOCK, ARCHIVED</td><td>Only approved/valid products become ACTIVE</td></tr>
<tr><td>RFQ</td><td>OPEN, QUOTED, ACCEPTED, EXPIRED, REJECTED</td><td>Only OPEN RFQs accept quotations</td></tr>
<tr><td>Quotation</td><td>PENDING, ACCEPTED, REJECTED</td><td>Accepting one quotation closes competing quotes</td></tr>
<tr><td>Order</td><td>PENDING, CONFIRMED, PROCESSING, SHIPPED, DELIVERED, CANCELLED</td><td>Prevent invalid backward transitions</td></tr>
<tr><td>Payment</td><td>PENDING, PAID, FAILED, REFUNDED, ESCROW_HOLD</td><td>Payment success comes from provider webhook</td></tr>
<tr><td>Ticket</td><td>OPEN, IN_PROGRESS, RESOLVED</td><td>Keep replies and status history</td></tr></table>

<h2>11. Error format</h2><pre>{
  "success": false,
  "message": "Validation failed",
  "errors": {
    "categoryId": "Category is required",
    "subcategoryId": "Subcategory does not belong to selected category"
  },
  "requestId": "req_123"
}</pre>
<p>Use 409 for duplicate category/subcategory/SKU, 422 for invalid business transitions, and return a request ID for tracing.</p>

<h2>12. Database and operational requirements</h2>
<pre>users
user_roles
addresses
categories
subcategories
products
product_images
product_variants
price_tiers
wishlists
rfqs
quotations
orders
order_items
payments
escrow_transactions
inventory
inventory_movements
conversations
messages
reviews
support_tickets
notifications
audit_logs</pre>
<p>Recommended unique constraints:</p><pre>UNIQUE categories.name
UNIQUE (subcategories.category_id, subcategories.name)
UNIQUE products.sku
INDEX products.category_id
INDEX products.subcategory_id
INDEX products.status
INDEX orders.buyer_id
INDEX orders.supplier_id
INDEX rfqs.status</pre>
<p>Use database transactions for quotation acceptance/order creation, product creation with inventory initialization, payment/escrow updates, and admin approval actions. Use idempotency keys for OTP, order, payment, quotation acceptance, notification dispatch, and webhook processing.</p>

<h2>13. End-to-end primary flows</h2>
<h3>Buyer purchases through RFQ</h3><pre>Login → Browse products → View product → Create RFQ → Supplier quotes
→ Compare quotations → Accept quotation → Create order → Create payment intent
→ Payment webhook → Order confirmed → Supplier processes → Shipment tracking
→ Delivery confirmation → Escrow release → Review product</pre>
<h3>Admin catalog setup</h3><pre>Admin login → Create Category with mandatory image
→ Create Subcategory under Category with mandatory image
→ Add Product using Category and Subcategory dropdowns
→ Upload product image → Submit product
→ Validate/approve product → Product becomes visible to buyers</pre>
<h3>Supplier selling flow</h3><pre>Supplier login → Complete KYC/GST → Add product → Admin approval
→ Receive RFQ lead → Submit quotation → Buyer accepts → Process order
→ Update shipment → Delivery → Settlement</pre>

<h2>14. Frontend-to-backend implementation notes</h2>
<ul><li>Frontend must not create categories automatically when creating a product.</li><li>Frontend must load subcategories after category selection and send both IDs.</li><li>Backend must independently verify every relationship and permission.</li><li>Category and Subcategory images are mandatory in the admin forms.</li><li>Product discount must be calculated by backend from MRP and selling price.</li><li>Admin count values such as productCount and subcategoryCount should be calculated by backend.</li><li>Use signed URLs or CDN URLs for image delivery and storage keys for replacement/deletion.</li><li>All admin changes should record actor, timestamp, previous value, new value, IP/device metadata where appropriate.</li></ul>
</body></html>
